      "id": "GENUS_INDICATOR",
      "name": "Indicator",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Drably plumaged birds with a remarkable behavioural adaptation — they guide humans and honey badgers to bee nests, then feed on the exposed wax and larvae after the nest is broken open. True to their scientific name, they are living indicators of wild bee colonies. They are brood parasites, laying their eggs in the nests of barbets, woodpeckers, and other cavity-nesting birds.",
